From 5f7b1a34823a18cf92b1b021cdcc9e9ae5fddb5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:55:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] state: FTS free gate frees nothing while any family is named;
 cross-process refusal memo; per-thread plans [daveey]

Review of the free-path gates (2026-11-19):
- integrity_check names a shared page against one owner only, so a path that frees one family's trees is unsafe
  whenever the plan names ANY family; the gate now detaches instead (reproduced: messages reused the freed page).
- a refused plan is remembered next to state.db (all processes), not per handle; memo hits log at debug.
- the attempt plan, startup and retry-tick flags are thread-local; without a plan the gate always skips.
- detach flips in-memory flags first, then commits breadcrumb + trigger drops in one transaction (retried 10 s).
- optimize_fts raises FtsFreeRefused, so vacuum() stops before VACUUM and `sessions optimize` exits 1.
- verified trash is keyed by root page; the old list format is re-verified.
- the gate checks the freed trees' roots are where the plan saw them.
- a detached store skips the trigram exclusion rebuild (its recovery recreates it from current DDL).
- backfill reports no work when only unverifiable trash remains.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
